<p>

Essential Eclipse Shortcuts for Productivity<br/><hr/>
Category	Shortcut	Action Description<br/><hr/>
Navigation	<strong>Ctrl + Shift + T</strong>	Open any Java type (class, interface) <br><hr>
<Strong>Ctrl + Shift + R</Strong>	Open any resource (file) <br><hr>
<strong>Ctrl + E </strong>	Switch between open editor tabs <br><hr>
<strong>Ctrl + O</strong>	Quick outline to show methods/fields of a class <br><hr>
<strong>Editing	Ctrl + 1	</strong>Quick Fix (fix errors, assign to variable, extract constant) <br/><hr/>
<strong>Ctrl + Space</strong>	Content Assist (autocomplete, generate code) <br><hr>
<strong>Ctrl + D	</strong>Delete the current line <br><hr>
<strong> Alt + ↑ / ↓ </strong>	Move a line or code block up or down <br><hr>
<strong>Ctrl + /	</strong>Toggle single-line comment <br/><hr/>
<strong>Ctrl + Shift + F</strong>	Format source code <br/><hr/>
<strong>Ctrl + I</strong>	Correct indentation for selected code <br/><hr/>
Refactoring	<strong>Alt + Shift + R	</strong>Rename a variable, method, or class <br/><hr/>
<strong>Alt + Shift + L	</strong>Extract selected expression to a local variable <br/><hr/>
<strong>Alt + Shift + M</strong>	Extract selected code to a method <br/><hr/>
<strong>Source & Run	 Ctrl + Shift + O </strong>	Organize imports <br><hr>
<strong>Alt + Shift + S  </strong>Open the source menu (generate getters/setters, constructors) <br/><hr/>
<strong>Ctrl  F11 	Run the last launched application  </strong>


</p>

